<h1>Roles &amp; Access</h1>

<div class="card">
  <h2>The three access levels</h2>
  <p>Roles are fixed — not a configurable permission matrix. This is what each one can already do.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Capability</th>
        <th>Employee</th>
        <th>Manager</th>
        <th>Admin</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>View own profile, request time off, see own payslips &amp; reviews</td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Approve direct reports' time off <small>(own reports only, not company-wide)</small></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>View team calendar &amp; team performance reviews</td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Manage People Directory, Payroll, Recruitment, Compliance, Reports</td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Assign access levels to employees</td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" disabled></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" checked disabled></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><small>Read-only — these checkboxes describe what each role can already do. A role that can't access a tab doesn't see it exist at all.</small></p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Assign access</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Employee</th><th>Title</th><th>Department</th><th>Access level</th><th></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @employees.each do |employee| %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= employee.full_name %></td>
          <td><%= employee.job_title %></td>
          <td><%= employee.department %></td>
          <td><%= employee.role.humanize %></td>
          <td>
            <% if employee.active? %>
              <%= link_to "Change", edit_roles_access_path(employee), class: "btn btn-ghost" %>
            <% else %>
              <span title="<%= employee.offboarding? ? "Offboarding in progress" : "Offboarded — access already revoked" %>">Change</span>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
